<!--
    arm64e virtual calls resolved by pointer-auth discriminator
    (`option arm64evcall on|off`).

    Issue: an arm64e C++ virtual call loads its target from a vtable slot and
    authenticates it with `blraa`/`braa`, so it renders as
    `(**(code **)(*obj + off))(...)` with no hint of the method. iOS 16.4.1
    debugserver has 295 such sites.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement. `analyzers/rtti/kuna_arm64evcall.rs`
    indexes every run of IA-signed, address-diversified `__const` slots by
    (index in run, diversifier) from the chained fixups, walks back from each
    call to its `movk #d, lsl #48` and the authenticated vtable-pointer load,
    and the flow builds the CALLIND as a direct call when the slot holds one
    method, or warns with the candidates when it holds several.

    P0 assertion: `option arm64evcall on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; every pass loads
    the `macho_arm64e_vcall` fixture (two vtables `{A_f, A_g}` and
    `{B_f, A_g}`, see the fixtures README) through the object bootstrap.

    Pass 1 (`option arm64evcall off`) reproduces the BUG: both calls are
    anonymous slot calls.
    Pass 2 (`option arm64evcall on`, the shipped default) is the FIX:
    `_call_g` calls `_A_g` (slot 1 holds it in both vtables) and `_call_f`
    names its two candidates.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
